; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR ELIZA v3  -  the 1966 chatbot, fast and conversational   (VM1 @ $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Type normally - lower case is fine. It asks your name first. BYE (or Esc) to quit.
;
;   > hello                   HELLO, CRAIG. WHAT'S ON YOUR MIND?
;   > my mother hates me      TELL ME MORE ABOUT YOUR FAMILY.
;   > i am sad                DID YOU COME TO ME BECAUSE YOU ARE SAD?
;   > i am sad                PLEASE DON'T REPEAT YOURSELF, CRAIG.
;   > whatever                EARLIER YOU SAID YOUR MOTHER HATES YOU.
;
; A rewrite of ELIZA v2 (none of its code is reused). New: type in any case;
; whole-word keywords by priority (100 keywords in 31 groups); 124 replies taken in
; turn; memory ("MY ..." comes back later); notices repeats; uses your name.
; A reply starts 6,000-49,000 1802 instructions after Enter - about 0.02-0.2 s
; (v2: up to 1.7 million, 7 seconds).
;
; THE SPLIT. The text work is native 1802 at $4C00 (Firmware-Math/eliza_native.asm,
; 866 bytes), entered with RUNMC and an operation letter at $6B00: P parse the
; line, N take the name, B fill in a reply. The conversation - which group to
; answer from, the rotation of replies, the memory, goodbye - is the STELLAR
; program below. Edit the script (keywords, replies, pronoun swaps) in
; Firmware-Math/build_eliza3.py, not here.
;
; MEMORY. SETSIZE 3 takes $4000-$6FFF, so load it with no other programs in
; the $5000 and $6000 blocks. Replies $5000-$5FFF, buffers $6000-$6FFF.
; Needs firmware with SETSIZE ($F2), RUNMC ($F1), PRINTSTR, GETSTR - V0061.28 on.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/eliza3_verify.py, V0061.33 image): conversations
; replayed against a Python model of the same rules, character for character -
; 33 scripted lines + 400 random lines, 0 wrong.
;
; RUN ON THE ELF2K 2026-09-24 (V0061.33) - Craig: "It is much faster. Well done."
;
; 136 STELLAR commands, $4000-$419C (413 bytes); native code $4C00-$4F61.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 F2 03          SETSIZE 3                          Take $4000-$6FFF: VM1 plus the two blocks above it
; D 4003 11 04 00 40    LOADXI R4 0040                     Every group starts on its first reply
; ZROT:
; D 4007 43 04          DECX R4
; D 4009 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 400C 2F 04 2B 10    WRITEIDX R4 2B10
; D 4010 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 4012 A1 00 07       IFFALSEI ZROT
; D 4015 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4019 2F 0E 2B 08    WRITEIDX R14 2B08                  Nothing remembered yet
; D 401D 2F 0E 21 00    WRITEIDX R14 2100                  and no previous line
; D 4021 11 0E 03 00    LOADXI R14 0300
; D 4025 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       HI, I'M ELIZA. WHAT'S YOUR NAME?
; D 4027 BD 00 E3       CALL INPUT
; D 402A 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 402E 10 00 4E       LOADAI 004E
; D 4031 2F 0E 2B 00    WRITEIDX R14 2B00
; D 4035 F1 4C 00       RUNMC 4C00                         Pick the name out of the reply
; D 4038 11 04 00 23    LOADXI R4 0023
; D 403C BD 01 4E       CALL SAY                           NICE TO MEET YOU, <name>. ...
; LOOP:
; D 403F BD 00 E3       CALL INPUT
; D 4042 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4046 10 00 50       LOADAI 0050
; D 4049 2F 0E 2B 00    WRITEIDX R14 2B00
; D 404D F1 4C 00       RUNMC 4C00                         Parse: words, repeat check, keyword, swapped fragment, MY
; D 4050 2E 0E 2B 04    READIDX R14 2B04                   Said "MY ..."? Remember it
; D 4054 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4057 A0 00 70       IFTRUEI NOMY
; D 405A 11 0D 24 00    LOADXI R13 2400
; D 405E 11 0E 26 00    LOADXI R14 2600
; D 4062 3B DE FF       COPYMXMY R13 R14 FF                MEM := MYF
; D 4065 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4069 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001
; D 406C 2F 0E 2B 08    WRITEIDX R14 2B08
; NOMY:
; D 4070 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4074 2E 0E 2B 03    READIDX R14 2B03
; D 4078 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 407B A0 00 85       IFTRUEI NOTEMPTY
; D 407E 11 04 00 21    LOADXI R4 0021                     An empty line
; D 4082 B0 00 C9       GAL ANSWER
; NOTEMPTY:
; D 4085 2E 0E 2B 02    READIDX R14 2B02
; D 4089 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 408C A0 00 96       IFTRUEI NOTREP
; D 408F 11 04 00 20    LOADXI R4 0020                     The same line twice
; D 4093 B0 00 C9       GAL ANSWER
; NOTREP:
; D 4096 2E 0E 2B 01    READIDX R14 2B01
; D 409A 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4                   R4 = the keyword group
; D 409C 86 04 00 FF    TESTXI R4 00FF
; D 40A0 A0 00 AD       IFTRUEI NOKEY
; D 40A3 86 04 00 00    TESTXI R4 0000
; D 40A7 A0 00 CF       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 40AA B0 00 C9       GAL ANSWER
; NOKEY:
; D 40AD 2E 0E 2B 08    READIDX R14 2B08                   Nothing matched: bring back the memory, if any
; D 40B1 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 40B4 A0 00 C5       IFTRUEI FALL
; D 40B7 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 40BA 2F 0E 2B 08    WRITEIDX R14 2B08
; D 40BE 11 04 00 22    LOADXI R4 0022
; D 40C2 B0 00 C9       GAL ANSWER
; FALL:
; D 40C5 11 04 00 1F    LOADXI R4 001F
; ANSWER:
; D 40C9 BD 01 4E       CALL SAY
; D 40CC B0 00 3F       GAL LOOP
; QUIT:
; D 40CF BD 01 4E       CALL SAY                           Goodbye
; D 40D2 11 0E 03 31    LOADXI R14 0331
; D 40D6 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       and a new line for the monitor
; D 40D8 00             HALT
; ESCQ:
; D 40D9 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 40DD B0 00 CF       GAL QUIT
; D 40E0 F0 00 00       BREAK                              End of program
; INPUT:
; D 40E3 11 0E 03 2A    LOADXI R14 032A
; D 40E7 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 40E9 11 0C 2C 00    LOADXI R12 2C00
; D 40ED 11 0D 2C 00    LOADXI R13 2C00
; D 40F1 BD 00 FC       CALL GETL                          Read the line (echoed; backspace works; a lone ESC first quits)
; D 40F4 11 0E 03 31    LOADXI R14 0331
; D 40F8 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 40FA BE 00          RETURN
; GETL:
; GETLK:
; D 40FC CB             SERIN                              the first key
; D 40FD 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B
; D 4100 A1 01 14       IFFALSEI GETLN
; D 4103 BD 01 38       CALL GETLW                         ESC: an arrow following?
; D 4106 A1 00 D9       IFFALSEI ESCQ                      no: ESC on its own quits
; D 4109 CB             SERIN                              an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 410A BD 01 38       CALL GETLW
; D 410D A1 00 FC       IFFALSEI GETLK
; D 4110 CB             SERIN
; D 4111 B0 00 FC       GAL GETLK
; GETLN:
; D 4114 81 00 0D       TESTAI 000D
; D 4117 A1 01 22       IFFALSEI GETLC
; D 411A 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 411D 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)      Enter alone: the empty line
; D 4120 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLC:
; D 4122 81 00 08       TESTAI 0008
; D 4125 A0 00 FC       IFTRUEI GETLK                      nothing to rub out yet
; D 4128 81 00 7F       TESTAI 007F
; D 412B A0 00 FC       IFTRUEI GETLK
; D 412E C9             SEROUT                             the echo
; D 412F 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)
; D 4132 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4134 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the rest of the line (Backspace can rub out the first key too)
; D 4136 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLW:
; D 4138 72 09          PUSHX R9
; D 413A 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008
; GETLW1:
; D 413E CC             SERST
; D 413F A0 01 49       IFTRUEI GETLW2
; D 4142 43 09          DECX R9
; D 4144 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 4146 A1 01 3E       IFFALSEI GETLW1
; GETLW2:
; D 4149 73 09          POPX R9
; D 414B CC             SERST                              Test: a key is waiting
; D 414C BE 00          RETURN
; SAY:
; D 414E 2E 04 0A 00    READIDX R4 0A00
; D 4152 21 05          COPYAX Acc -> R5                   R5 = the group's first reply
; D 4154 2E 04 2B 10    READIDX R4 2B10
; D 4158 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6                   R6 = where its rotation is
; D 415A 50 56 07       ADDXYZ R5 + R6 -> R7               R7 = the reply to use
; D 415D 2E 04 0A 40    READIDX R4 0A40
; D 4161 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8
; D 4163 42 06          INCX R6                            advance the rotation
; D 4165 89 68          TESTLXY R6 < R8
; D 4167 A0 01 6E       IFTRUEI SAY1
; D 416A 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000                     wrapping round
; SAY1:
; D 416E 22 06          COPYXA R6 -> Acc
; D 4170 2F 04 2B 10    WRITEIDX R4 2B10
; D 4174 50 77 09       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R9               R9 = 2 x reply: its pointer
; D 4177 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 417B 2E 09 0A 80    READIDX R9 0A80
; D 417F 2F 0E 2B 05    WRITEIDX R14 2B05
; D 4183 2E 09 0A 81    READIDX R9 0A81
; D 4187 2F 0E 2B 06    WRITEIDX R14 2B06
; D 418B 10 00 42       LOADAI 0042
; D 418E 2F 0E 2B 00    WRITEIDX R14 2B00
; D 4192 F1 4C 00       RUNMC 4C00                         Fill it in: * fragment, @ name, & memory
; D 4195 11 0E 28 00    LOADXI R14 2800
; D 4199 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 419B BE 00          RETURN

